I), as defined in the deck, is calculated as:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(488,19,'5. The “Value Chain” concept in the deck, under the philosophy “We are all Marketers,” refers to:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(489,19,'6. In the Critical Marketing Questions (CMQ) framework, “Where are we now?” is answered primarily through:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(490,19,'7. Externally, the macro environment is commonly analyzed using which framework, according to the deck?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(491,19,'8. The micro environment acronym “COSMIC” mentioned in the deck includes which of the following groups?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(492,19,'9. Niche marketing, as described in the deck, is best characterized by:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(493,19,'10. In Porter\'s Five Forces (used for competitor analysis in the deck), bargaining power of suppliers tends to be HIGH when:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(494,19,'11. Which of the following is NOT listed in the deck as a barrier for new entrants?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(495,19,'12. “Benchmarking,” as defined in the deck, refers to: A. Measuring a company\'s products, services, or performance against industry leaders or competitors to identify strengths and weaknesses','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(496,19,'13. SWOT analysis is used to evaluate which four elements?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(497,19,'14. TOWS (TWOS) analysis extends SWOT by developing four strategy types. Which pair below is correctly matched to its description?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(498,19,'15. In an EFAS (External Factor Analysis Summary) table, what must all assigned weights sum to, regardless of the number of factors?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(499,19,'16. On the EFAS rating scale described in the deck, a rating of 5 represents:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(500,19,'17. According to the deck, the total weighted score for an average firm in an industry (on an EFAS/IFAS analysis) is approximately:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(501,19,'18. Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) is most appropriate for analyzing trends over:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(502,19,'19. Which growth metric is best suited for evaluating the immediate, short-term impact of a one-week flash sale or promotional campaign?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(503,19,'20. A Moving Annual Total (MAT) is best described as:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(504,19,'21. Year-to-Date (YTD) growth measures cumulative performance from:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(505,19,'22. In the Product Life Cycle, the stage characterized by rapidly rising sales and profits, where the marketing objective is to build brand preference and increase sales volume, is:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(506,19,'23. During the Maturity stage of the Product Life Cycle, the marketing objective described in the deck is to:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(507,19,'24. Which positioning approach relies on a single, unique feature that differentiates a brand from every competitor in the market (Unique Selling Proposition)?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(508,19,'25. Positioning a brand using celebrities or influencers as endorsers, where the celebrity represents the target audience, is known as:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(509,19,'26. Hedonic (cultural/symbolic) positioning is based primarily on:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(510,19,'27. Which of the following correctly lists all 7 elements of the Marketing Mix (7P\'s) described in the deck?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(511,19,'28. What is the key difference between a brand\'s “slogan” and its “tagline,” according to the deck?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(512,19,'29. Pricing a product low at launch specifically to gain market share quickly is known as:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(513,19,'30. Setting an initially high price and gradually lowering it over time to capture profit from successive market layers is called:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(514,19,'31. Owning your own retail outlet directly (e.g., a brand operating its own stores) is an example of which type of vertical distribution channel?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(515,19,'32. A franchise arrangement, where a company licenses its name and equipment for a set period while the franchisee manages daily operations, falls under which channel of distribution strategy?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(516,19,'33. Under the Marketing Mix element of “Physical Evidence,” which of the following is explicitly mentioned as part of creating an effective service environment?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(517,19,'34. In the branding hierarchy described in the deck, which concept is built up FIRST, forming the foundation for brand identity, positioning, recognition, recall, personality, and loyalty?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(518,19,'35. “Brand recognition,” as defined in the deck, refers to:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(519,19,'36. “Brand recall” differs from “brand recognition” in that recall specifically refers to:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(520,19,'37. Which of the following best describes “positive brand equity” as outlined in the deck?','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(521,19,'38. In the Growth Strategy Matrix (Ansoff-style) described in the deck, selling EXISTING products to EXISTING markets is called:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(522,19,'39. Developing NEW products to sell to NEW markets, considered the riskiest of the four growth strategies, is known as:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13'),(523,19,'40. Finding new geographic markets or customer segments for an existing, unchanged product is an example of:','2026-06-21 07:51:13','2026-06-21 07:51:13');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `course_exam_questions` ENABLE KEYS */;
