كانت بسيطة؟',807,'ج) لمنع تكرار الحوادث مستقبلاً',1,'2026-06-15 14:12:01','2026-06-15 14:12:01'),(3909,275,484,'1. According to the deck, marketing is best defined as:',1666,'A. The process by which companies create customer superior added value and build strong customer relationships in order to capture value from customers in return',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3910,275,485,'2. In the “end results of marketing efforts” framework (A-S-L-P-G-R-M), what does the “M” stand for?',1672,'C. Market Share',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3911,275,486,'3. Which formula correctly represents Market Share as presented in the deck?',1675,'B. Total sales ÷ Total market sales × 100',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3912,275,487,'4. Return on Investment (ROI), as defined in the deck, is calculated as:',1678,'A. Net Income ÷ Total Cost × 100',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3913,275,488,'5. The “Value Chain” concept in the deck, under the philosophy “We are all Marketers,” refers to:',1683,'B. The series of internal departments (purchasing, design, production, marketing, selling, financing, recruiting, etc.) that work together to support and enhance the company\'s products and image',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3914,275,489,'6. In the Critical Marketing Questions (CMQ) framework, “Where are we now?” is answered primarily through:',1687,'B. Market situation analysis (macro and micro environment)',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3915,275,490,'7. Externally, the macro environment is commonly analyzed using which framework, according to the deck?',1691,'B. PESTEL',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3916,275,491,'8. The micro environment acronym “COSMIC” mentioned in the deck includes which of the following groups?',1694,'A. Customers, Organization, Suppliers, Market intermediaries, and Competitors',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3917,275,492,'9. Niche marketing, as described in the deck, is best characterized by:',1699,'B. A targeted strategy focusing on a specific, well-defined, narrow market segment',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3918,275,493,'10. In Porter\'s Five Forces (used for competitor analysis in the deck), bargaining power of suppliers tends to be HIGH when:',1703,'B. Suppliers are few in number and demand is high',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3919,275,494,'11. Which of the following is NOT listed in the deck as a barrier for new entrants?',1708,'C. Low switching costs for customers',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3920,275,495,'12. “Benchmarking,” as defined in the deck, refers to: A. Measuring a company\'s products, services, or performance against industry leaders or competitors to identify strengths and weaknesses',1710,'A. Measuring a company\'s products, services, or performance against industry leaders or competitors to identify strengths and weaknesses',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3921,275,496,'13. SWOT analysis is used to evaluate which four elements?',1715,'B. Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3922,275,497,'14. TOWS (TWOS) analysis extends SWOT by developing four strategy types. Which pair below is correctly matched to its description?',1718,'A. SO = maxi-maxi (use strengths to maximize opportunities)',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3923,275,498,'15. In an EFAS (External Factor Analysis Summary) table, what must all assigned weights sum to, regardless of the number of factors?',1723,'B. 1.00',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3924,275,499,'16. On the EFAS rating scale described in the deck, a rating of 5 represents:',1728,'C. Outstanding response to the factor',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3925,275,500,'17. According to the deck, the total weighted score for an average firm in an industry (on an EFAS/IFAS analysis) is approximately:',1732,'3',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3926,275,501,'18. Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) is most appropriate for analyzing trends over:',1736,'C. Three or more years',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3927,275,502,'19. Which growth metric is best suited for evaluating the immediate, short-term impact of a one-week flash sale or promotional campaign?',1739,'B. Previous Period Growth (Month-over-Month / Quarter-over-Quarter)',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3928,275,503,'20. A Moving Annual Total (MAT) is best described as:',1743,'B. A rolling sum of a metric over the most recent 12 consecutive months that updates monthly',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3929,275,504,'21. Year-to-Date (YTD) growth measures cumulative performance from:',1747,'B. The start of the calendar or fiscal year up to the present date',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3930,275,505,'22. In the Product Life Cycle, the stage characterized by rapidly rising sales and profits, where the marketing objective is to build brand preference and increase sales volume, is:',1751,'B. Growth',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3931,275,506,'23. During the Maturity stage of the Product Life Cycle, the marketing objective described in the deck is to:',1756,'C. Maximize market share and enter new markets',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3932,275,507,'24. Which positioning approach relies on a single, unique feature that differentiates a brand from every competitor in the market (Unique Selling Proposition)?',1759,'B. Product attribute positioning',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3933,275,508,'25. Positioning a brand using celebrities or influencers as endorsers, where the celebrity represents the target audience, is known as:',1763,'B. Product user positioning',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3934,275,509,'26. Hedonic (cultural/symbolic) positioning is based primarily on:',1767,'B. Creating an emotional/feeling attachment to the product since customers are not always rational',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3935,275,510,'27. Which of the following correctly lists all 7 elements of the Marketing Mix (7P\'s) described in the deck?',1770,'A. Product, Price, Place, Promotion, People, Process, Physical Evidence',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3936,275,511,'28. What is the key difference between a brand\'s “slogan” and its “tagline,” according to the deck?',1775,'B. A slogan is campaign-specific and short term, while a tagline is the brand\'s timeless, permanent identity phrase',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3937,275,512,'29. Pricing a product low at launch specifically to gain market share quickly is known as:',1780,'C. Penetration pricing',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3938,275,513,'30. Setting an initially high price and gradually lowering it over time to capture profit from successive market layers is called:',1784,'C. Competition pricing',0,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3939,275,514,'31. Owning your own retail outlet directly (e.g., a brand operating its own stores) is an example of which type of vertical distribution channel?',1788,'C. Ownership',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3940,275,515,'32. A franchise arrangement, where a company licenses its name and equipment for a set period while the franchisee manages daily operations, falls under which channel of distribution strategy?',1792,'C. Contractual (franchise)',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3941,275,516,'33. Under the Marketing Mix element of “Physical Evidence,” which of the following is explicitly mentioned as part of creating an effective service environment?',1794,'A. Sight, sound, scent, touch, and taste appeal',1,'2026-06-21 08:35:03','2026-06-21 08:35:03'),(3942,275,517,'34. In the branding hierarchy described in the deck, which concep