5130,326,189,'7. يمكن تفعيل العرض أونلاين من خلال:',596,'ب) Paymob Quick Link واختيار ValU Egypt',1,'2026-07-16 09:19:51','2026-07-16 09:19:51'),(5131,326,190,'8. خلال فترة العرض يمكن استخدام التيرمين على مدد من:',600,'ب) 12 إلى 24 شهر',0,'2026-07-16 09:19:51','2026-07-16 09:19:51'),(5132,327,484,'1. According to the deck, marketing is best defined as:',1666,'A. The process by which companies create customer superior added value and build strong customer relationships in order to capture value from customers in return',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:01','2026-07-20 08:36:01'),(5133,327,485,'2. In the “end results of marketing efforts” framework (A-S-L-P-G-R-M), what does the “M” stand for?',1672,'C. Market Share',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:01','2026-07-20 08:36:01'),(5134,327,486,'3. Which formula correctly represents Market Share as presented in the deck?',1675,'B. Total sales ÷ Total market sales × 100',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:01','2026-07-20 08:36:01'),(5135,327,487,'4. Return on Investment (ROI), as defined in the deck, is calculated as:',1678,'A. Net Income ÷ Total Cost × 100',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5136,327,488,'5. The “Value Chain” concept in the deck, under the philosophy “We are all Marketers,” refers to:',1685,'D. The external supply chain run entirely by suppliers',0,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5137,327,489,'6. In the Critical Marketing Questions (CMQ) framework, “Where are we now?” is answered primarily through:',1687,'B. Market situation analysis (macro and micro environment)',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5138,327,490,'7. Externally, the macro environment is commonly analyzed using which framework, according to the deck?',1691,'B. PESTEL',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5139,327,491,'8. The micro environment acronym “COSMIC” mentioned in the deck includes which of the following groups?',1694,'A. Customers, Organization, Suppliers, Market intermediaries, and Competitors',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5140,327,492,'9. Niche marketing, as described in the deck, is best characterized by:',1699,'B. A targeted strategy focusing on a specific, well-defined, narrow market segment',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5141,327,493,'10. In Porter\'s Five Forces (used for competitor analysis in the deck), bargaining power of suppliers tends to be HIGH when:',1703,'B. Suppliers are few in number and demand is high',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5142,327,494,'11. Which of the following is NOT listed in the deck as a barrier for new entrants?',1708,'C. Low switching costs for customers',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5143,327,495,'12. “Benchmarking,” as defined in the deck, refers to: A. Measuring a company\'s products, services, or performance against industry leaders or competitors to identify strengths and weaknesses',1710,'A. Measuring a company\'s products, services, or performance against industry leaders or competitors to identify strengths and weaknesses',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5144,327,496,'13. SWOT analysis is used to evaluate which four elements?',1715,'B. Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5145,327,497,'14. TOWS (TWOS) analysis extends SWOT by developing four strategy types. Which pair below is correctly matched to its description?',1718,'A. SO = maxi-maxi (use strengths to maximize opportunities)',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5146,327,498,'15. In an EFAS (External Factor Analysis Summary) table, what must all assigned weights sum to, regardless of the number of factors?',1722,'A. 10.00',0,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5147,327,499,'16. On the EFAS rating scale described in the deck, a rating of 5 represents:',1728,'C. Outstanding response to the factor',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5148,327,500,'17. According to the deck, the total weighted score for an average firm in an industry (on an EFAS/IFAS analysis) is approximately:',1732,'3',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5149,327,501,'18. Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) is most appropriate for analyzing trends over:',1736,'C. Three or more years',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5150,327,502,'19. Which growth metric is best suited for evaluating the immediate, short-term impact of a one-week flash sale or promotional campaign?',1739,'B. Previous Period Growth (Month-over-Month / Quarter-over-Quarter)',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5151,327,503,'20. A Moving Annual Total (MAT) is best described as:',1743,'B. A rolling sum of a metric over the most recent 12 consecutive months that updates monthly',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5152,327,504,'21. Year-to-Date (YTD) growth measures cumulative performance from:',1747,'B. The start of the calendar or fiscal year up to the present date',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5153,327,505,'22. In the Product Life Cycle, the stage characterized by rapidly rising sales and profits, where the marketing objective is to build brand preference and increase sales volume, is:',1751,'B. Growth',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5154,327,506,'23. During the Maturity stage of the Product Life Cycle, the marketing objective described in the deck is to:',1756,'C. Maximize market share and enter new markets',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5155,327,507,'24. Which positioning approach relies on a single, unique feature that differentiates a brand from every competitor in the market (Unique Selling Proposition)?',1759,'B. Product attribute positioning',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5156,327,508,'25. Positioning a brand using celebrities or influencers as endorsers, where the celebrity represents the target audience, is known as:',1763,'B. Product user positioning',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5157,327,509,'26. Hedonic (cultural/symbolic) positioning is based primarily on:',1767,'B. Creating an emotional/feeling attachment to the product since customers are not always rational',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5158,327,510,'27. Which of the following correctly lists all 7 elements of the Marketing Mix (7P\'s) described in the deck?',1770,'A. Product, Price, Place, Promotion, People, Process, Physical Evidence',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5159,327,511,'28. What is the key difference between a brand\'s “slogan” and its “tagline,” according to the deck?',1775,'B. A slogan is campaign-specific and short term, while a tagline is the brand\'s timeless, permanent identity phrase',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5160,327,512,'29. Pricing a product low at launch specifically to gain market share quickly is known as:',1781,'D. Bundle pricing',0,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5161,327,513,'30. Setting an initially high price and gradually lowering it over time to capture profit from successive market layers is called:',1783,'B. Skimming pricing',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5162,327,514,'31. Owning your own retail outlet directly (e.g., a brand operating its own stores) is an example of which type of vertical distribution channel?',1788,'C. Ownership',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5163,327,515,'32. A franchise arrangement, where a company licenses its name and equipment for a set period while the franchisee manages daily operations, falls under which channel of distribution strategy?',1792,'C. Contractual (franchise)',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5164,327,516,'33. Under the Marketing Mix element of “Physical Evidence,” which of the following is explicitly mentioned as part of creating an effective service environment?',1794,'A. Sight, sound, scent, touch, and taste appeal',1,'2026-07-20 08:36:02','2026-07-20 08:36:02'),(5165,327,517,'34. In the branding hierar