 rating of 5 represents:',1728,'C. Outstanding response to the factor',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5348,332,500,'17. According to the deck, the total weighted score for an average firm in an industry (on an EFAS/IFAS analysis) is approximately:',1732,'3',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5349,332,501,'18. Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) is most appropriate for analyzing trends over:',1736,'C. Three or more years',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5350,332,502,'19. Which growth metric is best suited for evaluating the immediate, short-term impact of a one-week flash sale or promotional campaign?',1739,'B. Previous Period Growth (Month-over-Month / Quarter-over-Quarter)',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5351,332,503,'20. A Moving Annual Total (MAT) is best described as:',1742,'A. A one-time snapshot taken only at the end of the fiscal year',0,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5352,332,504,'21. Year-to-Date (YTD) growth measures cumulative performance from:',1747,'B. The start of the calendar or fiscal year up to the present date',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5353,332,505,'22. In the Product Life Cycle, the stage characterized by rapidly rising sales and profits, where the marketing objective is to build brand preference and increase sales volume, is:',1751,'B. Growth',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5354,332,506,'23. During the Maturity stage of the Product Life Cycle, the marketing objective described in the deck is to:',1756,'C. Maximize market share and enter new markets',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5355,332,507,'24. Which positioning approach relies on a single, unique feature that differentiates a brand from every competitor in the market (Unique Selling Proposition)?',1759,'B. Product attribute positioning',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5356,332,508,'25. Positioning a brand using celebrities or influencers as endorsers, where the celebrity represents the target audience, is known as:',1763,'B. Product user positioning',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5357,332,509,'26. Hedonic (cultural/symbolic) positioning is based primarily on:',1767,'B. Creating an emotional/feeling attachment to the product since customers are not always rational',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5358,332,510,'27. Which of the following correctly lists all 7 elements of the Marketing Mix (7P\'s) described in the deck?',1770,'A. Product, Price, Place, Promotion, People, Process, Physical Evidence',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5359,332,511,'28. What is the key difference between a brand\'s “slogan” and its “tagline,” according to the deck?',1775,'B. A slogan is campaign-specific and short term, while a tagline is the brand\'s timeless, permanent identity phrase',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5360,332,512,'29. Pricing a product low at launch specifically to gain market share quickly is known as:',1780,'C. Penetration pricing',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5361,332,513,'30. Setting an initially high price and gradually lowering it over time to capture profit from successive market layers is called:',1783,'B. Skimming pricing',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5362,332,514,'31. Owning your own retail outlet directly (e.g., a brand operating its own stores) is an example of which type of vertical distribution channel?',1788,'C. Ownership',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5363,332,515,'32. A franchise arrangement, where a company licenses its name and equipment for a set period while the franchisee manages daily operations, falls under which channel of distribution strategy?',1792,'C. Contractual (franchise)',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5364,332,516,'33. Under the Marketing Mix element of “Physical Evidence,” which of the following is explicitly mentioned as part of creating an effective service environment?',1794,'A. Sight, sound, scent, touch, and taste appeal',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5365,332,517,'34. In the branding hierarchy described in the deck, which concept is built up FIRST, forming the foundation for brand identity, positioning, recognition, recall, personality, and loyalty?',1798,'A. Brand loyalty',0,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5366,332,518,'35. “Brand recognition,” as defined in the deck, refers to:',1802,'A. A consumer\'s ability to correctly identify a product or service just by viewing its logo, tagline, packaging, or ad campaign',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5367,332,519,'36. “Brand recall” differs from “brand recognition” in that recall specifically refers to:',1807,'B. The likelihood of instantly remembering a brand\'s name when thinking of its product type or category',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5368,332,520,'37. Which of the following best describes “positive brand equity” as outlined in the deck?',1810,'A. A combination of positive image, positive reputation, and positive attitude toward the brand',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5369,332,521,'38. In the Growth Strategy Matrix (Ansoff-style) described in the deck, selling EXISTING products to EXISTING markets is called:',1816,'C. Market penetration',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5370,332,522,'39. Developing NEW products to sell to NEW markets, considered the riskiest of the four growth strategies, is known as:',1821,'D. Diversification',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5371,332,523,'40. Finding new geographic markets or customer segments for an existing, unchanged product is an example of:',1822,'A. Market development',1,'2026-07-20 09:05:27','2026-07-20 09:05:27'),(5372,333,246,'ما المقصود بالسلامة والصحة المهنية (OSH)؟',770,'ب) حماية صحة وسلامة ورفاهية العاملين',1,'2026-07-20 14:28:56','2026-07-20 14:28:56'),(5373,333,247,'أي مما يلي يُع