:',1666,'A. The process by which companies create customer superior added value and build strong customer relationships in order to capture value from customers in return',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5473,343,485,'2. In the “end results of marketing efforts” framework (A-S-L-P-G-R-M), what does the “M” stand for?',1671,'B. Margin',0,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5474,343,486,'3. Which formula correctly represents Market Share as presented in the deck?',1675,'B. Total sales ÷ Total market sales × 100',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5475,343,487,'4. Return on Investment (ROI), as defined in the deck, is calculated as:',1678,'A. Net Income ÷ Total Cost × 100',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5476,343,488,'5. The “Value Chain” concept in the deck, under the philosophy “We are all Marketers,” refers to:',1683,'B. The series of internal departments (purchasing, design, production, marketing, selling, financing, recruiting, etc.) that work together to support and enhance the company\'s products and image',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5477,343,489,'6. In the Critical Marketing Questions (CMQ) framework, “Where are we now?” is answered primarily through:',1687,'B. Market situation analysis (macro and micro environment)',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5478,343,490,'7. Externally, the macro environment is commonly analyzed using which framework, according to the deck?',1691,'B. PESTEL',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5479,343,491,'8. The micro environment acronym “COSMIC” mentioned in the deck includes which of the following groups?',1694,'A. Customers, Organization, Suppliers, Market intermediaries, and Competitors',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5480,343,492,'9. Niche marketing, as described in the deck, is best characterized by:',1699,'B. A targeted strategy focusing on a specific, well-defined, narrow market segment',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5481,343,493,'10. In Porter\'s Five Forces (used for competitor analysis in the deck), bargaining power of suppliers tends to be HIGH when:',1703,'B. Suppliers are few in number and demand is high',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5482,343,494,'11. Which of the following is NOT listed in the deck as a barrier for new entrants?',1708,'C. Low switching costs for customers',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5483,343,495,'12. “Benchmarking,” as defined in the deck, refers to: A. Measuring a company\'s products, services, or performance against industry leaders or competitors to identify strengths and weaknesses',1710,'A. Measuring a company\'s products, services, or performance against industry leaders or competitors to identify strengths and weaknesses',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5484,343,496,'13. SWOT analysis is used to evaluate which four elements?',1715,'B. Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5485,343,497,'14. TOWS (TWOS) analysis extends SWOT by developing four strategy types. Which pair below is correctly matched to its description?',1718,'A. SO = maxi-maxi (use strengths to maximize opportunities)',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5486,343,498,'15. In an EFAS (External Factor Analysis Summary) table, what must all assigned weights sum to, regardless of the number of factors?',1723,'B. 1.00',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5487,343,499,'16. On the EFAS rating scale described in the deck, a rating of 5 represents:',1728,'C. Outstanding response to the factor',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5488,343,500,'17. According to the deck, the total weighted score for an average firm in an industry (on an EFAS/IFAS analysis) is approximately:',1732,'3',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5489,343,501,'18. Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) is most appropriate for analyzing trends over:',1736,'C. Three or more years',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5490,343,502,'19. Which growth metric is best suited for evaluating the immediate, short-term impact of a one-week flash sale or promotional campaign?',1739,'B. Previous Period Growth (Month-over-Month / Quarter-over-Quarter)',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5491,343,503,'20. A Moving Annual Total (MAT) is best described as:',1743,'B. A rolling sum of a metric over the most recent 12 consecutive months that updates monthly',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5492,343,504,'21. Year-to-Date (YTD) growth measures cumulative performance from:',1747,'B. The start of the calendar or fiscal year up to the present date',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5493,343,505,'22. In the Product Life Cycle, the stage characterized by rapidly rising sales and profits, where the marketing objective is to build brand preference and increase sales volume, is:',1751,'B. Growth',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5494,343,506,'23. During the Maturity stage of the Product Life Cycle, the marketing objective described in the deck is to:',1756,'C. Maximize market share and enter new markets',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5495,343,507,'24. Which positioning approach relies on a single, unique feature that differentiates a brand from every competitor in the market (Unique Selling Proposition)?',1759,'B. Product attribute positioning',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5496,343,508,'25. Positioning a brand using celebrities or influencers as endorsers, where the celebrity represents the target audience, is known as:',1763,'B. Product user positioning',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'),(5497,343,509,'26. Hedonic (cultural/symbolic) positioning is based primarily on:',1767,'B. Creating an emotional/feeling attachment to the product since customers are not always rational',1,'2026-07-21 08:35:41','2026-07-21 08:35:41'